      <bioghist id="aspace_3c87c90fc63fc2c4623715cb209dbddb">
         <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
         <p>Peter Ford was born in 1937 and is an engraver from Bristol, England. He graduated from the Brighton College of Art (now the University of Sussex) and taught art and English from 1961 to 1976. Largely self-taught as a printmaker, he has been the artistic director at Off-Centre Gallery, Bristol, since 1987, with a focus on international art on paper. Ford is a fellow of the Royal Society of Painter-Printmakers, a member of the Royal West of England Academy, and a member of the International Association of Papermaking Artists.</p>
      </bioghist>
      <prefercite id="aspace_433e945708ffcd48e40db331ea17ba0c">
